<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  folio-assistant — getting started: from "create a folio" to a live site.

  Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other
  BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it
  by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.

  The shape of this process is an argument about one sentence. "Create a folio"
  is asked by at least five different people wanting five different things:

    new-repo      never used folio-assistant, wants a folio in a fresh repo
    overlay       has a repository already, wants folio-assistant laid over it
    add-folio     is already in a layer, wants a second folio at top level
    new-content   is already in a folio, and meant a DOCUMENT, not a folio
    ask           the filesystem cannot tell, so the agent must

  Gateway_Intent does NOT let the agent pick. It carries <cat-harness.processes:decision/>, so
  the branch is computed by decisions/folio-intent.dmn from three facts, one of
  which is what the user actually said. `ask` is one of the outcomes the table
  can return — which is what makes asking obligatory rather than polite.

  Gateway_Live is the same construction applied to publication: `live`,
  `not-yet` and `unknown` are three states, and the third is never dressed up as
  either of the others. A fourth, `unprovisioned`, is checked before them: no
  gh-pages branch exists, so Pages cannot be switched on to serve it. Every
  publishing path (new-repo, overlay, add-folio, and an overlay or new repo that
  remote-mounts its dependencies) passes Task_ProvisionGhPages before
  Task_PagesBootstrap, and `unprovisioned` routes back to it.

  Enforcement is strict. Three steps are non-relaxable and each for the same
  kind of reason — they are the points where the process is acting on somebody
  else's repository or on their behalf:

    Task_ReadFacts       scaffolding without looking first is how a folio gets
                         written over somebody's project
    Gateway_Intent       the triage itself; relaxing it lets the agent guess
    Task_ConfirmImport   nobody's files are moved or imported on inference
    Task_ChooseHarnessed nothing in the repository is declared to the harness
                         on inference: the scan suggests, the person picks

  The <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill
  that implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared
  work plan in beans/.
-->
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns/"
                  id="Definitions_GettingStarted"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="onboarding-agent" name="Onboarding agent"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="publish-target" name="Publish target"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="user" name="User"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="work-plan" name="Work plan (beans)"/>
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_GettingStarted">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_GettingStarted" name="Getting started — &quot;create a folio&quot; to a live site" processRef="Process_GettingStarted" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_GettingStarted" name="Getting started" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Somebody said "create a folio": work out which request they meant, with the branch computed by a decision table that may answer "ask", and what has to be true before anything is written, through to a live site.

      "Create a folio" is five different requests. Gateway_Intent computes which one
      from decisions/folio-intent.dmn rather than letting the agent assume, and `ask`
      is one of the outcomes the table can return. Gateway_Live applies the same
      construction to publication, with `unknown` kept distinct from `not-yet`.

      Source of truth: this file. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is
      generated from it by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="strict" />
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="Process_GettingStarted_LaneSet">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_User" name="User (person)" partitionElementRef="user">
        <bpmn:documentation>Answers the one question Gateway_Intent cannot compute for itself — "ask" is one of five outcomes decisions/folio-intent.dmn can return — and, only on the overlay path, the questions a repo scan cannot answer on its own: which of the content markers it found the harness should declare (Task_ChooseHarnessed), then what to import, where it goes, and who does the importing.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>StartEvent_AskToStart</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_AskIntent</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ChooseHarnessed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ConfirmImport</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Onboarding agent (system)" partitionElementRef="onboarding-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>Every write in this diagram belongs to this lane, and each sits behind the non-relaxable read-first gate: nothing is created or scaffolded until Gateway_Intent has classified what was actually asked for.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_DetectModality</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReadFacts</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Intent</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ScanRepo</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_CreateRepo</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_HandOff</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Scaffold</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_SeedPlan</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_BeanOpen</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_BeanYours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_BeanNotYours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Publish" name="Publish — GitHub Pages" partitionElementRef="publish-target">
        <bpmn:documentation>Provisions the gh-pages branch before Pages is switched on (Task_ProvisionGhPages), derives the URL, and holds the report that follows it: "unprovisioned" routes back to provisioning, and "live", "not-yet" and "unknown" are exclusive branches of one DMN-computed gateway, so a failed probe is reported as "unknown", never as "not-yet".</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ProvisionGhPages</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_PagesBootstrap</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Live</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReportUrl</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReportPending</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReportUnknown</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_Ready</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_BeanClose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_AskToStart" name="&quot;create a folio&quot;">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_DetectModality" name="Detect the interaction
modality">
      <bpmn:documentation>Before the first question is asked, establish HOW to ask it: audio, ordinary chat, selectable options for a user with limited hand function, large-type for low vision. A user who finds the questions unusable never reaches the rest of this diagram.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="interaction-modality" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ReadFacts" name="Read the repository
facts">
      <bpmn:documentation>Mechanical, read-only: does the layer's config (its `index.config.json` entry; a legacy `&lt;name&gt;.config.json` only as a fallback) declare a contentType, does the working tree hold somebody's existing project, and what has the user actually said. These are the three inputs to folio-intent.dmn. Non-relaxable: scaffolding without looking first is how a folio gets written over somebody's project.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <cat-harness.processes:policy relaxable="false" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_answer</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Intent" name="What is the user
asking for?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Computed, not chosen. decisions/folio-intent.dmn returns one of five branches from statedIntent, isFolio and repoHasContent. Non-relaxable.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <cat-harness.processes:policy relaxable="false" />
        <cat-harness.processes:decision ref="decisions/folio-intent.dmn#Decision_FolioIntent" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ask</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_overlay</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_newrepo</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_newcontent</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_addfolio</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_AskIntent" name="Choose from the
offered options">
      <bpmn:documentation>The question is presented as a short list of selectable options, never as free prose, and the list names the top-level content types the agent knows about. The answer becomes the statedIntent fact and the table is evaluated again — the user's answer is read as evidence, like any other fact.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="interaction-modality" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ask</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_answer</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ScanRepo" name="Scan the repo for
content worth importing">
      <bpmn:documentation>Read-only. Classifies candidates into library/ (external source) and content/ (authored here), and reports what it could not classify as its own bucket rather than forcing every file into one of the two. Its fourth section, `markers`, lists the content markers it found — sushi-config.yaml, a legacy dak.json, .bpmn processes, a beans store, library/, Lean, folio manifests — each with its paths, whether index.config.json already declares it (declared, not-declared, or unknown), and the snippet that would. `bun run cat-harness-tools/scripts/scan-repo-content.ts --json`, a plain command any agent host can run.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="repo-conversion" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-intake" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_overlay</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_scan</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_ChooseHarnessed" calledElement="Process_AskThePerson" name="Choose what the
harness reads">
      <bpmn:documentation>A PERSON'S STEP: the scan's `markers` that are not yet declared are offered as selectable options — one per marker, each with its paths and what declaring it means, plus "none of these" — and the person picks which parts of the repository to load into the KG. A tap card where the host has one; otherwise a numbered pick-list with a stated default. Never a typed reply. The default declares NOTHING. Only the picks reach Task_Scaffold, which declares exactly those in index.config.json. With no undeclared marker found, nothing is asked. The same question is put after setup by running the scan with `--markers` (repo-conversion §2a).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <cat-harness.processes:policy relaxable="false" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="repo-conversion" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="interaction-modality" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_scan</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_chosen</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>

    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_ConfirmImport" name="Import what, where,
and who does it">
      <bpmn:documentation>Three questions the scan cannot answer: import these or not; library or content for each group; leave the files where they are or reorganize to declutter. Plus whether to dispatch one ingestion agent or a small swarm. Non-relaxable: nobody's files are moved or imported on inference.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <cat-harness.processes:policy relaxable="false" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="repo-conversion" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="dispatch-agent" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_chosen</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_confirm</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_CreateRepo" name="Create the
repository">
      <bpmn:documentation>Only on the new-repo branch, and only after the user has named it. An empty working directory is scaffolded in place instead.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="repo-conversion" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_newrepo</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_created</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_HandOff" name="Handed to content
authoring">
      <bpmn:documentation>The misspeak case. The user has a folio and wants a document in it; this process ends and authoring-a-document.bpmn or authoring-a-paper.bpmn begins.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_newcontent</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Scaffold" name="Scaffold the folio
(folio_init)">
      <bpmn:documentation>content/, uploads/, library/, the first manifests, &lt;slug&gt;.json and index.config.json (the layer's config inline in its entry; no &lt;slug&gt;.config.json), the builder shim, AGENTS.md with its stubs, .mcp.json, the session-start hook and the beans store. On the overlay path it declares in index.config.json exactly the markers picked at Task_ChooseHarnessed, and none it was not given. Refuses rather than overwrites when a folio is already present.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_addfolio</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_confirm</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_created</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_seed</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_SeedPlan" name="Seed the work plan">
      <bpmn:documentation>The first beans: what the author said they want to get started on, one bean per top-level content object they named.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager" />
        <cat-harness.processes:bean op="note"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_provision</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:dataOutputAssociation id="DOA_Task_SeedPlan">
        <bpmn:targetRef>DSR_work_plan</bpmn:targetRef>
      </bpmn:dataOutputAssociation>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ProvisionGhPages" name="Provision gh-pages">
      <bpmn:documentation>Before Pages is switched on, make sure the gh-pages branch exists — the semantics of A_Provision in bootstrap-tools' render-kg-to-github-pages.bpmn, first half. `git ls-remote --heads origin gh-pages`; if absent, `bun run cat-harness/scripts/pages-bootstrap.ts --provision` pushes an orphan gh-pages holding a placeholder index.html and .nojekyll (idempotent; never forced; the script creates no remote branch without the flag). Then Settings → Pages → "Deploy from a branch: gh-pages, / (root)" — not "GitHub Actions" when the publish workflow pushes gh-pages. Every publishing path reaches this step: new-repo, overlay and add-folio, and an overlay or new repo that remote-mounts its dependencies.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_provision</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_unprovisioned</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_pages</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_PagesBootstrap" name="Start the Pages build
and derive the URL">
      <bpmn:documentation>scripts/pages-bootstrap.ts: check the gh-pages branch first (absent is `unprovisioned`), derive the site URL from the git remote or the layer's config (its index.config.json entry), report whether a publish workflow exists and the Pages source it needs, and optionally probe until the site answers.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_pages</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_probe</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Live" name="Is the site
answering?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Computed from decisions/pages-live-gate.dmn. Four outcomes: `unprovisioned` (no gh-pages branch — back to Task_ProvisionGhPages) is checked first, and `unknown` is not a softer `not-yet`.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <cat-harness.processes:decision ref="decisions/pages-live-gate.dmn#Decision_PagesLive" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_probe</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_live</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_notyet</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_unknown</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_unprovisioned</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ReportUrl" name="Hand over the
live link">
      <bpmn:documentation>Confirmed live. The link is given as a link, and the author is told what is on it.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_live</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_done1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ReportPending" name="Say where it
will be">
      <bpmn:documentation>A measured 404. The author is told the address and that the first build has not landed there yet.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_notyet</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_done2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ReportUnknown" name="Say it could not
be confirmed">
      <bpmn:documentation>No URL, no probe, or a failed request. Reported as "could not check", never as "not yet" and never as "live".</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="getting-started" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_unknown</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_done3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_Ready" name="Ready to author">
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_4</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_BeanOpen" name="Open the bean" calledElement="Process_BeanOpen">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn; the gateway after this reads which end it reached.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="bean-coordination"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_seed</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_BeanYours" name="Bean claimed?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_BeanNotYours" name="Not yours —&#10;left alone">
      <bpmn:documentation>Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_BeanClose" name="Close the bean" calledElement="Process_BeanClose">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn; placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_done1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_done2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_done3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="StartEvent_AskToStart" targetRef="Task_DetectModality" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="Task_DetectModality" targetRef="Task_ReadFacts" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" sourceRef="Task_ReadFacts" targetRef="Gateway_Intent" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ask" name="ask" sourceRef="Gateway_Intent" targetRef="Task_AskIntent" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_answer" sourceRef="Task_AskIntent" targetRef="Task_ReadFacts" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_overlay" name="overlay" sourceRef="Gateway_Intent" targetRef="Task_ScanRepo" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_newrepo" name="new-repo" sourceRef="Gateway_Intent" targetRef="Task_CreateRepo" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_newcontent" name="new-content" sourceRef="Gateway_Intent" targetRef="EndEvent_HandOff" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_addfolio" name="add-folio" sourceRef="Gateway_Intent" targetRef="Task_Scaffold" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_scan" sourceRef="Task_ScanRepo" targetRef="Task_ChooseHarnessed" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_chosen" sourceRef="Task_ChooseHarnessed" targetRef="Task_ConfirmImport" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_confirm" sourceRef="Task_ConfirmImport" targetRef="Task_Scaffold" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_created" sourceRef="Task_CreateRepo" targetRef="Task_Scaffold" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_seed" sourceRef="Task_Scaffold" targetRef="Call_BeanOpen" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_provision" sourceRef="Task_SeedPlan" targetRef="Task_ProvisionGhPages" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_pages" sourceRef="Task_ProvisionGhPages" targetRef="Task_PagesBootstrap" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_probe" sourceRef="Task_PagesBootstrap" targetRef="Gateway_Live" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_live" name="live" sourceRef="Gateway_Live" targetRef="Task_ReportUrl" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_notyet" name="not-yet" sourceRef="Gateway_Live" targetRef="Task_ReportPending" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_unknown" name="unknown" sourceRef="Gateway_Live" targetRef="Task_ReportUnknown" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_unprovisioned" name="unprovisioned" sourceRef="Gateway_Live" targetRef="Task_ProvisionGhPages" />
